# User uploads are data, never code.
#
# Upload handlers (App\Utils\Util::uploadFile, App\Media::uploadFile,
# Util::storeRemoteFile) already store files under a safe extension derived
# from the detected content type. This is a backstop for Apache: refuse to
# serve anything with a script extension from this tree, in case such a file
# ever gets here some other way. (nginx / IIS / `php artisan serve` ignore
# this file; configure the equivalent there.)
<FilesMatch "(?i)\.(php[0-9]?|phtml|phar|pht|phps|cgi|pl|py|sh|asp|aspx|jsp)$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# Do not list directory contents.
Options -Indexes
